messages.content:
{
  "thought_process": "Your line (555-123-2002) is Active on our side, so “No SIM card detected” points to a device-side SIM recognition issue. When the SIM isn’t detected, the phone can’t register to the network, which explains both “No Signal” and “Data Disabled.” The fastest fixes are to reseat the SIM, then re-check whether the phone recognizes it. If it’s still missing, we’ll reboot and test again. If it remains missing after that, we’ll isolate whether it’s a SIM card problem or a phone SIM-tray/reader issue.",
  "next_steps_on_device": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Reseat the SIM",
      "actions": [
        "Run reseat_sim_card (this simulates removing and reinserting the SIM).",
        "Wait ~15 seconds.",
        "Run check_sim_status and tell me the result (Active, Missing, or Locked)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "If SIM is still Missing after reseat",
      "actions": [
        "Run reboot_device to fully restart the phone.",
        "After it boots, run check_sim_status again and share the result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "If SIM becomes Active",
      "actions": [
        "Watch for signal bars to appear and a network type (4G/5G).",
        "If the status bar still shows Data Disabled, toggle_data ON again.",
        "Try a quick test call and let me know if it connects."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "If SIM remains Missing after reboot",
      "actions": [
        "If possible, test your SIM in another phone, or test another known‑working SIM in your Galaxy S21. This helps pinpoint whether the issue is with the SIM card or the phone’s SIM reader.",
        "Report what you find so I can advise the next step. If the SIM itself appears faulty or the phone can’t read any SIM, I’ll arrange the appropriate next action."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "If the SIM ever shows Locked, stop and tell me—don’t attempt PIN/PUK guesses; that requires security assistance.",
    "Your line shows roaming enabled, but since you’re in Austin, TX, roaming shouldn’t be a factor here."
  ],
  "please_report_back": [
    "Result of check_sim_status after Step 1 (and after reboot if needed).",
    "If it becomes Active: whether signal bars returned and if a test call works."
  ]
}

