      "title": "Do you have a SIM tray?",
      "instructions": [
        "Look at the phone’s edges for a tiny pinhole next to a thin tray. If you see that, you have a physical SIM. If you do NOT see any tray (just smooth edges), your phone likely uses an eSIM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "If you DO have a SIM tray: reseat the SIM",
      "instructions": [
        "Power the phone OFF.",
        "Use the SIM tool (or a small paperclip) to gently press into the pinhole and eject the tray.",
        "You should see a small card on the tray. Without changing its orientation, remove it, then place it back flat and snug.",
        "Reinsert the tray fully until it’s flush.",
        "Turn the phone back ON and wait up to 2 minutes. Check if the “SIM missing” message is gone and if signal bars appear."
      ],
      "reassurance": "This won’t erase anything; it just helps the phone re-read the SIM."
