messages.content:
{
  "message": "Yes — Airplane Mode turns off all wireless connections (cellular, data, Wi‑Fi), so MMS cannot send while it’s ON. The first and most important step is to turn Airplane Mode OFF.",
  "reassurance": "Turning Airplane Mode off/on will not delete any of your photos or messages.",
  "thought_process": "MMS requires cellular service and mobile data. With Airplane Mode ON, those are disabled. We’ll turn it OFF, then confirm mobile data works, then test an MMS.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Turn OFF Airplane Mode",
      "iphone": "Open Settings > toggle Airplane Mode OFF. Or open Control Center (swipe down from the top‑right) and tap the airplane icon so it is not highlighted.",
      "android": "Swipe down from the top twice to open Quick Settings and tap the airplane icon so it’s OFF. Or go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) and toggle Airplane mode OFF.",
      "confirm": "You should see the ✈️ airplane icon disappear from the top of your screen."
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify mobile data works",
      "do": "With Wi‑Fi still OFF for this test, make sure Mobile/Cellular Data is ON (Settings > Cellular/Mobile Data on iPhone; Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network on Android). Then open your browser and go to example.com.",
      "result": "Tell me if the page loads over mobile data."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test sending an MMS to yourself",
      "do": "Open your messaging app and send a small photo to your own number. Note whether it sends successfully, keeps spinning, or shows an error."
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "After turning Airplane Mode OFF, did the airplane icon disappear?",
    "Did example.com load over mobile data?",
    "What happened when you sent a photo to yourself?"
  ],
  "next_if_needed": [
    "If it still fails after Airplane Mode is OFF and data works, we’ll briefly turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling (if enabled) and try again.",
    "If needed after that, we’ll reset the phone’s APN (carrier data/MMSC) settings to default and reboot. This won’t delete photos or messages."
  ]
}

