messages.content:
{
  "message": "“No Signal” explains why MMS won’t send—your phone currently isn’t connected to the cellular network. That’s not expected once Airplane Mode is OFF, so we’ll quickly restore service. Nothing we’ll do will delete photos or messages.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs cellular service and mobile data. With No Signal, we’ll first verify the SIM is recognized, then refresh network settings and the connection. After signal returns, we’ll re-test MMS.",
  "reassurance": "Turning Wi‑Fi, data, Wi‑Fi Calling, or rebooting on/off will not erase any photos or messages.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Turn Wi‑Fi back ON (optional, just to stay online)",
      "do": "Turn Wi‑Fi ON so you remain connected to the internet while we fix cellular. MMS still won’t send until we regain signal."
    },
    {
      "title": "Check SIM status",
      "why": "If the phone doesn’t see the SIM, it can’t connect to the network.",
      "how": "Please run the diagnostic: check_sim_status and tell me the result (Active, Missing, or Locked).",
      "what_to_do_based_on_result": [
        "Active: Good—go to the next step.",
        "Missing: Run reseat_sim_card to reseat the SIM virtually, then check again. Tell me if it changes.",
        "Locked: Do not guess PIN/PUK. Tell me it says Locked so I can get you to a human agent for SIM unlock assistance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Refresh your network mode and connection",
      "why": "Ensures the phone is allowed to use modern networks and forces a fresh registration.",
      "how": [
        "Set network preference to 4g_5g_preferred using set_network_mode_preference.",
        "Restart the phone using reboot_device."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "After restart: confirm signal",
      "do": "Look at the top bar: do you now see signal bars and a network type like 5G/LTE/4G? If yes, turn Wi‑Fi OFF briefly and try loading example.com to confirm mobile data works, then send a small photo MMS to yourself."
    }
  ],
  "identify_phone_type_if_needed": {
    "instructions": "If you’d like to know your phone type: open Settings. If you see ‘About phone’ (often under System), it’s Android. If you see Settings > General > About, it’s iPhone."
  },
  "questions": [
    "What does check_sim_status show (Active, Missing, or Locked)?",
    "After the reboot, do you see signal bars and a network type (5G/4G/LTE)?",
    "If you have signal, did example.com load over mobile data and did the MMS to yourself send?"
  ],
  "next_if_needed": [
    "If SIM is Active and there’s still No Signal after the reboot, we’ll try one more network refresh and then consider escalating.",
    "If signal returns but MMS still fails, we’ll quickly check/reset APN (carrier/MMSC) settings and retry."
  ]
}

