{
  "message": "Great—your SIM is now active. The “2G” part is likely why MMS won’t send. MMS needs at least 3G, and works best on 4G/LTE/5G. We’ll switch your phone to prefer 4G/5G, then test. Nothing in these steps will delete your photos or messages.",
  "thought_process": "Your line is active with data remaining. Your phone is currently on 2G (old/slow). Setting the network mode to prefer 4G/5G should restore proper data for MMS.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Make sure Mobile Data is ON and keep Wi‑Fi OFF for this test",
      "why": "MMS uses mobile data.",
      "do": "Confirm Mobile/Cellular Data is ON in Settings. Leave Wi‑Fi OFF just for the test."
    },
    {
